# Authorization Rules

Role != subscription != entitlement.

A user may be authenticated and still have no subscription (`currentPlan = null`).
That is distinct from being subscribed to Basic.

Use capability checks such as:
- can(user, permission)
- requirePermission(user, permission)
- requireEntitlement(user, entitlement)

`control_panel.access` requires a stored subscription.
Plan-specific feature flags stay separate.

Public discovery (AgriService Expert, Services, Transport, published products, published courses, published provider pages) does not require a publishing plan.
Publishing and management of public provider, marketplace, AgriService offerings and instructor-published courses require an eligible stored Pro, Business or Enterprise subscription (internal slug `professional` is Pro). Express this through entitlements; never scatter plan-name checks in UI or business logic.

Never hardcode subscription names inside UI/business logic.
Never treat a missing plan as Basic.
Never use browser/local cache as the source of truth for subscription or authorization.
Server-side authorization is mandatory.
UI permission checks only control presentation.
Enforce authorization at the server/action/API layer and at RLS where applicable.
